  "slug": "diana-microrna-cb45",
  "summary": "miRTarBase 11.0 and MIsoTEx show regulatory reference data now organized by experimental assay, tissue and isoform abundance.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the construction of structured resources that make regulatory and transcript evidence interpretable across assays and tissues. miRTarBase 11.0 organizes experimentally supported miRNA-target interactions around the approach that generated each record, reflecting that different experimental methods capture distinct interaction types. MIsoTEx and IsoAtlas apply comparable logic to transcript isoforms: MIsoTEx classifies mammalian isoforms by tissue distribution, expression stability and abundance, while IsoAtlas provides interactive visualization of long-read isoforms across 1035 human and 414 mouse samples. MEAM-OWL brings motif enrichment and motif copy number versus gene expression correlation into a browser-based setting. The RNA-seq benchmark differs in data type, reporting alignment errors and quantification bias for tandemly duplicated genes in model and crop plants under TopHat2, HISAT2 and STAR.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
